course: dictionary
lesson: 10231
title: Toddler, a word for keeping little ones safe
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A toddler is a young child who has just learned to walk, usually about one to three years old. Read the words around «toddler» to check: a child who has just learned to walk is small and still learning about the world.
explain: The sentences show what toddlers do. «A toddler in Texas swallowed a button battery from a TV remote» tells you toddlers put things in their mouths, so the battery was dangerous. «A toddler who has gone quiet is often getting into something dangerous, so go and check» tells you a quiet toddler needs an adult to look.
explain: Words help us stay safe. Toddler gate is a gate that keeps a toddler away from the stairs. Toddler group is a group where toddlers and their grown-ups play together. When you meet a new word in a safety text, ask: what does it tell me to do?
fact: A toddler is a young child who has just learned to walk.
fact: A toddler is usually about one to three years old.
fact: «Toddler» is a noun. You can say a toddler or toddlers.
fact: Toddlers explore by touching things and putting them in their mouths, so keep button batteries, medicines and cleaning products away.
fact: Never leave a toddler alone near water, even in a bath. Use stair gates, and tell an adult if a toddler is in danger.
exercise: «A toddler in Texas swallowed a button battery.» What is a toddler? | An old man who lives alone | *A young child who has just learned to walk | A kind of small dog | A teenager who is learning to drive
exercise: «He did it, the glass cracked, and a toddler inside screamed.» Find and copy the word that names a very young child. | screamed | cracked | *toddler | glass
exercise: Why should button batteries be kept away from toddlers? | Toddlers are too heavy to lift them | Button batteries make toddlers sleepy | Toddlers only like to play with batteries that are empty | *Toddlers may put them in their mouths and be badly hurt
test: How old is a toddler, usually? | About ten to twelve years old | *About one to three years old | Under one year old | About five to seven years old
test: As an older child, what can you do to help keep a toddler safe? | Leave the stair gate open | Give the toddler small toys to chew | *Close the gate and pick up small toys | Leave the bath full and walk away
exam: Which phrase means the stage of growing up from a very young child to a teenager? | *From toddler to teenager | Toddler group | Toddler gate | Toddler's tantrum
